!! Usage

# Provides a calendar widget, use it like `<$calendar />`
# Use the whole wiki as a data source, aggregate tiddler based on their `created` `modified` `startDate` and `endDate` field
# Drag to create new event with `startDate` and `endDate` field
# Provides a calendar view, use `ctrl+shift+L` to switch to this view, you can click {{$:/core/images/standard-layout}}{{$:/language/PageTemplate/Name}} button to go back to standard story river layout
# Add `color` field to change color. When `color` field missing, it will try get color from tags on it.

!! Developing Sub-Plugin

See [[Official wiki|https://tiddly-gittly.github.io/tiddlywiki-calendar/]].


!! Event records from a filter

Use `eventFilter` to supply FullCalendar event JSON records without creating one tiddler per event. The widget provides `calendarStart` and `calendarEnd` as UTC TiddlyWiki timestamps for the visible range (start inclusive, end exclusive).

With Activity Log Tools installed:

```wikitext
<$calendar filter="[all[]limit[0]]" eventSources="" eventFilter="[tag[$:/Tags/ActivityLog]activityevents<calendarStart>,<calendarEnd>]" />
```

Timestamp and interval logs display recorded times; daily count and RLE logs display all-day counts. Clicking a check-in opens its log. Changes to log tiddlers refresh the calendar.


!! Medicine check-ins in Events Calendar

Install Activity Log Tools and Health Tracker to enable the Medicine check-ins source automatically. In Control Panel → Settings → Calendar → Calendar data sources, select or clear its checkbox. Check-in logs do not need a `calendarEntry` field.

Select the 1-day view in the toolbar or the default view setting. Daily counts and date-only history appear in the all-day section.

!! Registering calendar data sources

Plugins provide tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/Calendar/EventSource`. Their `caption` and `description` fields appear in settings and support WikiText; `filter` returns FullCalendar event JSON records. For example:

```wikitext
title: $:/my-plugin/calendar/Checkins
tags: $:/tags/Calendar/EventSource
caption: Check-ins
description: Show daily check-in records.
filter: [tag[$:/Tags/ActivityLog]activityevents<calendarStart>,<calendarEnd>]
```

Sources in both regular and shadow tiddlers are discovered automatically. Filters receive `currentTiddler` as the source tiddler and `calendarStart` / `calendarEnd` as the visible range. Disabled source titles are saved in the `list` field of `$:/plugins/linonetwo/tw-calendar/settings/disabledEventSources`; all other sources are enabled by default.

`<$calendar />` loads enabled sources by default. An embedded calendar can set `eventSources=""` to disable discovery or use an `eventSources` filter to select source tiddlers. The additional event filter accepts custom events, and the event tiddler filter selects regular events. Search view only displays search results.
